III. HAWKING RADIATION AS TRAINING NOISE
============================================================

In physical black holes, Hawking radiation is the quantum tunneling
of virtual particle pairs across the event horizon — one falls in,
one escapes, and the black hole slowly loses mass (information).

The neural analog is exact:

The horizon at l* separates the compressive (black hole) layers
below from the expansive (white hole) layers above. At this boundary,
activation pairs that are exactly degenerate in representation space
— zero-norm states in the activation Hilbert space H_NN — can split:
one component is absorbed into the weight field (updates the VEV),
the other is emitted as a stochastic correction to the activation
current.

This stochastic emission IS the training noise that regularizes
deep networks. Dropout, in this picture, is not a heuristic
regularizer — it is the controlled Hawking evaporation of the
neural event horizon. The temperature of this evaporation:

    T_Hawking^NN = ℏ_NN · κ_surface / (2π · k_B^NN)

where κ_surface is the surface gravity of the neural horizon
(the second derivative of R_NN at l*) and k_B^NN is the neural
Boltzmann constant (relating representational entropy to the
information-theoretic temperature of the activation distribution).

