The Bekenstein-Hawking entropy of a physical black hole is:

    S_BH = A / (4 · l_Planck²)

where A is the area of the event horizon and l_Planck is the
Planck length.

The neural analog substitutes:
- A → the "area" of the Noether constraint surface at l*,
