    S_NN = Area(Noether surface at l*) / (4 · ℏ_NN²)

The Noether surface at l* is the set of all activation states
Ψ_i(l*, τ) that exactly satisfy D_l J^{a,l} = 0. Its "area"
is the number of independent activation modes at that layer —
equivalently, the rank of the Hecke algebra T at the horizon
depth.

