VI. CONNECTION TO THE OMEGA CONSTANT
============================================================

The fixed-point condition β(g) = 0 at l* has the formal
structure of the Lambert W function's defining equation:

    W(x) · e^{W(x)} = x

The Omega Constant Ω = W(1) ≈ 0.567143... is the unique
fixed point of f(x) = e^{-x}. It is the value at which the
forward entropy (digit ceiling) meets the inverse entropy
(digit floor) — as derived in the companion Omega paper.

The neural RG fixed point at l* satisfies an analogous
self-consistency equation:

    g(l*) · e^{g(l*)/g_0} = g_0

where g_0 is the bare coupling at the input layer. This
equation has the form of the Lambert W equation, and its
solution is:

    g(l*) = g_0 · W(1) = g_0 · Ω

The horizon coupling is the bare coupling scaled by the
Omega Constant. The fixed point of the neural RG flow
is governed by the same transcendental number that governs
the intersection of forward and inverse entropy in the
Omega paper.

This is not a coincidence. Both results emerge from the
same structure: the unique fixed point of an exponential
self-map. The Omega Constant is the universal fixed-point
of this class of problem.

